# Tea towel red (ticket 28.6): the west side's gingham tea towel, red and cream, draped over the bread box's lid and down its +x side (60 times life size). It
# is built in the bread box's own frame (origin the box's middle on y = 0, turned by the same yaw) and placed at the box's position, so the level turns both alike. A cloth 0.2 m
# thick lies on the deck (y 12.6 to 12.8, x 3.4 to 12.2, z -1.8 to 6.7, clear of the steel pull) and hangs 6 m down the wall's outer face (x 12.0 to 12.2, to y 6.8) round a
# rounded bend. Gingham: cream cloth (kitchen_gingham_cream) with a grid of stripes 0.8 m wide every 1.6 m in team_red_cloth (materials/buildings/, the team's cloth, kept out of
# materials/kitchen/ whose test allows no red or blue); the stripes are the cloth's own shape cut by repeated bars, a little proud of the cream. No collider.
format 1
collider none
shadows near

Detail detail=0.07
    Union
        Material material=kitchen_gingham_cream
            Subtraction
                Translate translation=(7.8, 9.8, 2.45)
                    RoundBox size=(4.40, 3.00, 4.25) roundness=0.5
                Translate translation=(3.5, 6.3, 2.45)
                    RoundBox size=(8.5, 6.30, 6) roundness=0.3
        Material material=team_red_cloth
            Intersection
                Subtraction
                    Translate translation=(7.8, 9.8, 2.45)
                        RoundBox size=(4.45, 3.05, 4.3) roundness=0.5
                    Translate translation=(3.5, 6.3, 2.45)
                        RoundBox size=(8.45, 6.25, 6) roundness=0.3
                Xor
                    Repetition spacing=(0, 0, 1.6)
                        Box size=(60, 60, 0.4)
                    Union
                        Intersection
                            Repetition spacing=(1.6, 0, 0)
                                Box size=(0.4, 60, 60)
                            Translate translation=(0, 16, 0)
                                Box size=(60, 4, 60)
                        Intersection
